From a923c9619a5918659aa0b0ea931deda46a05205f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evolution BR811 <344454957+Evolution-BR811@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:58:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Import SID files (C64 music)

PSID and RSID tunes are run on a small C64 (6502, SID, CIA/raster
interrupts, the KERNAL IRQ routines) and converted like NSF tracks:
editable patterns on the C64 channels, with instruments for the voice
settings (waveform, ADSR, ring/sync, filter routing) and macros for what
changes during a note and while it fades out.

- non-linear pitch and a tuning fitted to the player's frequency table,
  so every frequency comes out exact
- the filter and volume belong to the note that owns them (macros), and
  go to the pattern in notes longer than a macro
- the player's hard restart becomes Furnace's (envelope reset time and
  values), with 1Axx for notes without it
- a pulse width that runs freely across notes goes to the pattern
  (3xxx, 22xx/23xx) when that saves many instruments
- the track picker of the NSF import is used for SID subtunes

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
